      ":question/problem": "$\\sqrt{1.5}=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[2]{1.5},$ we get $x=1.5,$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{1.5}=\\sqrt[2]{1.5}={1.5}^{1/2}\n$$",
